<section class="learning-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2>The Four Principles of Action Design</h2>
    <p>Use these principles to understand why a small, well-designed action can outperform an ambitious but unclear intention.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="principles-grid">
    <article class="principle-card">
      <div class="principle-number">01 / SPECIFICITY</div>
      <h3>Make the action observable</h3>
      <p>Replace broad intentions with a behavior someone could see or verify. “Work on my career” is vague. “Compare three job descriptions” is observable.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle-card">
      <div class="principle-number">02 / CAPACITY</div>
      <h3>Match the action to available resources</h3>
      <p>Time, attention, energy, tools, and knowledge all affect what is realistic. Design the next step around actual capacity rather than an ideal day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle-card">
      <div class="principle-number">03 / FRICTION</div>
      <h3>Make starting easier</h3>
      <p>Remove avoidable obstacles before the work begins. Prepare the document, materials, workspace, or first instruction in advance.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle-card">
      <div class="principle-number">04 / FEEDBACK</div>
      <h3>Close the action loop</h3>
      <p>Record what happened. Completion, delay, and difficulty are useful information for improving the next action.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="execution-model">
  <div class="execution-panel">
    <div class="execution-header">
      <h2>The Execution Sequence</h2>
      <span>INTENTION → EVIDENCE</span>
    </div>
    <div class="execution-flow">
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-number">01</div>
        <strong>Identify</strong>
        <p>Choose the area that matters now.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-number">02</div>
        <strong>Assess</strong>
        <p>Check your time and capacity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-number">03</div>
        <strong>Reduce</strong>
        <p>Define the smallest useful step.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-number">04</div>
        <strong>Execute</strong>
        <p>Begin and complete the action.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-number">05</div>
        <strong>Review</strong>
